argument is $\theta(t)=2t$, so $n(\eta,0)=4\pi/(2\pi)=2$; correspondingly,
$(2\pi i)^{-1}\int_\gamma(2/z)\,dz=2$. The arrows indicate direction; the
labels record traversal multiplicity. The proof above is independent of this
illustration.

